    {
      "title": "Only the ledger sets items aside",
      "narrative": "Reserve route hands the items to Reservation ledger, the only part that changes a reservation; Release route goes through it too. In one transaction, the ledger locks each item's row in Stock DB, checks that the count minus what is already reserved covers the order, and writes the reservation. Because the check and the write happen under the same lock, no other order can change those rows in between.",
