    {
      "title": "The last item goes to the first order",
      "narrative": "Two shoppers can press Pay for the last item at the same moment. Whichever order locks the item's row first reserves it and commits. The second order waits at the lock until then, and finds nothing left. If even one of an order's items is short, the ledger reserves none of them, and Reserve route answers Checkout API with 409 sold out instead of 201 reserved.",
